# Files Vercel must NOT serve on the public production site.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel deploys this repo as a static site, which means every file in it is
# fetchable at https://www.fantasystudio.in/<path> unless excluded here. This
# list keeps source, internal, and authorization-model files off the public
# domain. (Vercel is the only deploy target — the GitHub Pages mirror and its
# workflow were removed in Jul 2026.)
#
# Pattern syntax is .gitignore-style. Anything listed here is omitted from the
# deployment bundle; it does not affect the git repo or local dev.

# Version control / tooling internals
.git
.github/
.claude/
.gitignore
.vercelignore

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Source & internal docs — never site assets. This is what keeps the root
# firestore.rules (and any nested docs) off the public domain.
# Vercel only applies the bare patterns to root-level files (verified live in
# Jul 2026), so every pattern needs an explicit **/ recursive twin.
*.md
**/*.md
*.rules
**/*.rules
*.rules.proposed
**/*.rules.proposed
*.local.md
**/*.local.md

# Scratch prototypes. _cptest.html is a standalone mock of the panel — no
# Firebase, no config, no real data — but it was still fetchable at
# /_cptest.html with no <title> and no noindex, so nothing stopped a crawler
# indexing an untitled prototype under the business's own domain. It is not in
# the sitemap and robots.txt only disallows /admin/ /client/ /team/ /studio/.
_cptest.html
**/_cptest.html
*.test.html
**/*.test.html

# NOTE: firebase-config.js is intentionally NOT excluded — the site needs it at
# runtime, and a Firebase web config is public by design (it is not a secret;
# the security boundary is firestore.rules, deployed in the Firebase console).
